This README file contains information on the contents of the meta-de1soc-fpga layer.

Please see the corresponding sections below for details.

Purpose
=======

Programs the FPGA fabric automatically at every Linux boot — no JTAG, no
Quartus Programmer, no manual step. A couple of seconds into boot the fabric
is configured with the music-player system (Nios II + shared RAM + bridges)
and the hps_music_player daemon can start against live hardware.

Contents
========

  conf/layer.conf
  recipes-bsp/fpga-autoload/fpga-autoload.bb
  recipes-bsp/fpga-autoload/files/
      soc_system.rbf       Compiled FPGA bitstream (raw binary format,
                           generated from the Quartus .sof)
      fpga-load.dtbo       Device tree overlay that triggers the FPGA
                           manager to program the rbf
      fpga-load.service    systemd oneshot unit that applies the overlay

How it works
============

fpga-load.service runs early (After=local-fs.target, DefaultDependencies=no)
and is ordered Before=hps_music_player.service, guaranteeing the fabric is
operating before the daemon maps the bridge window. It applies the overlay
through configfs:

  mkdir -p /sys/kernel/config/device-tree/overlays/fpga
  cat /lib/firmware/fpga-load.dtbo > .../overlays/fpga/dtbo

The kernel FPGA manager then loads /lib/firmware/soc_system.rbf referenced
by the overlay. Verify on the board:

  cat /sys/class/fpga_manager/fpga0/state   # operating
  cat /sys/class/fpga_bridge/br1/state      # enabled
  systemctl status fpga-load.service        # active (exited)

Requires the HPS-FPGA bridge nodes enabled in the DTB (done by the
post-build DTB patch step) and iomem=relaxed on the kernel command line.

Updating the bitstream
======================

1. Recompile the hardware in Quartus (with the embedded Nios II firmware,
   see 09MakeSof.sh) and convert the .sof to .rbf:

     quartus_cpf -c -o bitstream_compression=on output_files/<project>.sof soc_system.rbf

2. Replace recipes-bsp/fpga-autoload/files/soc_system.rbf
3. Rebuild:  bitbake fpga-autoload -c cleansstate && bitbake fpga-autoload
             bitbake core-image-minimal

Dependencies
============

  URI: https://github.com/altera-fpga/gsrd-socfpga.git
  branch: scarthgap

  (provides the poky, meta-intel-fpga, and supporting layers this layer
   builds on top of; no other project layers are required)

Adding the meta-de1soc-fpga layer to your build
===============================================

Run 'bitbake-layers add-layer meta-de1soc-fpga'

Then install the recipe in conf/local.conf:

  IMAGE_INSTALL:append = " fpga-autoload"

Patches
=======

This is a project-internal layer for the DE1-SoC FPGA Music Player
(TEC Computer Engineering). It is not submitted upstream.
